course: dictionary
lesson: 10653
title: Universal: true for everyone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Universal means true for, done by or belonging to everyone or everything, in every place. When you meet it, ask who or what it describes, and whether it covers everyone. «Temujin united the Mongol tribes and in 1206 was named Genghis Khan, meaning universal ruler.» A ruler who rules everyone, everywhere, is a universal ruler.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Water dissolves more substances than almost any other liquid, that is why it is called the universal solvent.» The words almost any other liquid tell you that universal means it works in a huge range of cases. Try your meaning in the sentence: it still makes sense.
explain: Universal can also describe things that work in all cases. «A universal charger fits many devices.» The word many is your clue, so universal means it works with lots of different things, not just one.
explain: Some uses are names rather than descriptions. «In the UK the BBFC rates films: U (Universal, for everyone).» Here the U rating tells you the film is for everyone of any age. The context shows you what the word is doing.
fact: Universal means true for everyone, or done by everyone, in every place.
fact: A «universal remote» works with any TV, so it works in many cases.
fact: «Universal laws of nature» belong to the whole universe, and gravity is one that works everywhere.
fact: Water is called the universal solvent because it dissolves more substances than almost any other liquid.
fact: The 1948 «Universal Declaration of Human Rights» says that every person has the same basic rights.
exercise: «Temujin was named Genghis Khan, meaning universal ruler.» What does universal mean here? | *Ruling over everyone, everywhere | Ruling with a very loud voice | Ruling over one small village | Ruling only in the winter
exercise: A universal remote works with any TV. What does universal suggest? | It only works with one TV | It is made of wood | It is broken and needs mending | *It works in many cases, with lots of devices
exercise: «The BBFC rates a film U, Universal, for everyone.» Which people is a U film for? | Only children who are older than ten | *Everyone, of any age | Only people who like cartoons | Only grown-ups over eighteen
test: In science, gravity is called universal because it works where? | Only in the sky | Only on Tuesdays | Only on Earth | *Everywhere
test: Nadia says universal means special for one person. Why is she wrong? | Universal means the same as lonely | Universal means very small and quiet | *Universal means true for everyone, not just one person
exam: Which sentence uses universal to mean true for everyone? | Water is wet, so it is always cold | The universal remote is in the drawer, under the sofa | *Everyone has universal human rights, so nobody is left out | Our school bus is blue and goes to the park
